# Every shared wallpaper link renders from one page; share.html reads the id out
# of the path. Status 200 rewrites instead of redirecting, so the URL the friend
# sees stays the one that was shared -- which is also the URL Android matches
# against the App Links intent filter.
#
# Two Cloudflare Pages behaviours shape this line:
#   * Pages canonicalises /<name>.html to /<name>, so the destination is written
#     WITHOUT the extension. Targeting /share.html made Pages answer the rewrite
#     with a 308 to /share, turning the rewrite back into a redirect.
#   * The page must not be called w.html either: /w.html folds to /w, and every
#     /w/<id> request then collapsed into /w with the id thrown away.
/w/*  /share  200
